le can  look into and enjoy my opinion can't  nothing make you forget it  each time you start from scratch what  voice is this that speaks within me when  did you first touch my heart they guide  you on your way I tried to be kind it  only made me colder  while use of voiceover in film is often  criticized as a crutch for bad writing  Malick's use of voiceover serves to  accompany more than to restate plot  characters are often using or observing  and you get the feeling that the  voice-over is almost more for the  character than it is for the audience  Malik's approach to voiceover is similar  to his approach to cinematography he's  there to observe not construct  [Music]  this interior landscape is naturally  subjective and it's reinforced by the  perspective of the narrative Malick's  stays with the characters that the story  focuses on rarely zooming out to a  broader perspective to inform the  audience the audience gets to know what  the characters know or care about and do  but not much more you're there with them  and rarely do we even get a wide shot or  an establishing shot to crown the  character within the world rather the  focus is on the characters subjective  experience of the environment around  them  the one time in badlands where we do get  a bird's-eye view perspective of what's  happening away from the protagonists  it's cast in an oddly stylized  black-and-white montage almost as if  we're seeing from Holly's perspective in  the future how she imagined things  happened in the past and this  subjectivity is I think what leads to  Malik's emphasis on nature and  environment as a part of this  storytelling this will become a much  heavier focus and play a larger role in  later films but it's very present in  badlands the film's title itself speaks  to this approach to filmmaking after the  characters experience the environment is  the next focus again taking priority  over plot and narrative the film's don't  emphasize locations rather they try to  